@startuml
!include _style.iuml
' Speaker note: Problem: deliver committed chat changes to all connected authorized sessions in a group.
' Speaker note: Candidates: polling clients, or group-scoped callback observers with SSE delivery.
' Speaker note: Choice: RealtimeHub fans out after commit; durable message replay uses realtime_events, not hub memory.
title Design class view · Chat event delivery
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ClassStereotypeFontSize 19
skinparam ranksep 35
class "chat-routes.ts\nPOST handlers" as POST <<publisher>> {
  createChatMessage(...)
  toggleChatReaction(...)
}
class RealtimeHub <<subject>> #F5F2E9 {
  - subscribers: Map<string, Set<RealtimeEventWriter>>
  + subscribe(groupId, writer): () => void
  + publish(event): void
  + subscriberCount(groupId?): number
}
interface "RealtimeEventWriter\n(function type)" as OBS <<observer>> #EEE7F3 {
  (event: ChatMessageEvent | ChatReactionEvent): void
}
class "chat-routes.ts\nSSE callback" as SSE <<concrete observer>> #F5F2E9 {
  writeEvent(event)
  writeReaction(event)
  subscribeToGroup(listener)
}
class "chat/index.ts" as CHAT <<module>> {
  + createChatMessage(...)
  + listChatEvents(...)
}
class realtime_events <<table>> #FCF7E7 {
  id: BIGINT <<PK>>
  message_id: TEXT <<FK, UNIQUE>>
}
POST -right-> RealtimeHub : publish after commit
RealtimeHub "1" o-right- "0..*" OBS : group writers
SSE .up.|> OBS
SSE -left-> RealtimeHub : subscribe / unsubscribe
POST -down-> CHAT : persist
CHAT -right-> realtime_events : message events
SSE -left-> CHAT : listChatEvents\n(Last-Event-ID)
legend bottom
  Each HTTP runtime owns one RealtimeHub; writers are callbacks, not observer classes.
  Messages replay from realtime_events. Reactions do not move the replay cursor.
endlegend
@enduml
